{"id":"word:hebrew:H2600","type":"word","title":"חִנָּם","subtitle":"H2600 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"gratis , i.e. devoid of cost, reason or advantage","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חִנָּם (H2600) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 32 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חִנָּם (chinnâm) means gratis , i.e. devoid of cost, reason or advantage First listed occurrence: 1Chr 21 24."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חִנָּם","transliteration":"chinnâm","pronunciation":"khin-nawm'","strong":"H2600","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2600","partOfSpeech":"adv","forms":["חִנָּ֑ם","חִנָּֽם","חִ֝נָּ֗ם","חִנָּ֔ם","חִנָּ֖ם"],"morphs":[["HD",31],["HTi/D",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"gratis , i.e. devoid of cost, reason or advantage","usage":"without a cause (cost, wages), causeless, to cost nothing, free(-ly), innocent, for nothing (nought, in vain.","full":"H2600. chinnam חִנָּם substantive , used chiefly in the accusative as adverb (compare Assyrian annáma , in vain , Dl K 7, Pr 44 ; from הֵּן , with aff. םָ֯ , which is sometimes found in substantives proper, as סֻלָּם , and proper names, but is more particularly used with substantives applied adverbially, as רֵיקָם דּוּמָם, אָמְנָם, יוֺמָם : Sta § 203 Ba NB § 216 ) — literally out of favour; i.e. a. gratis, gratuitously, for nothing , חִנָּם עָבַד to serve for nought Gen 29:15 ; Job 1:9 ; Isa 52:3 to be sold (figurative) for nought 52:5 ; Exod 21:2 , 11 חִנָּם יָצָא to go out(from slavery) freely, for nothing , Num 11:5 which we used to eat in Egyptian for nought, Jer 22:13 ; 1Chr 21:24 ; in the Genitive 2Sam 24:24 חִנָּם עֹלוֺת i.e. burnt-offerings which cost nothing (in the || 1Chr 21:24 the construction is changed). b. for no purpose, in vain Prov 1:17 ; Mal 1:10 : once חִנָּם אֶל (compare אֶל 7 ) Ezek 6:10 . c. gratuitously, without cause, undeservedly , especially of groundless hostility or attack, 1Sam 19:5 חִנָּם לְהָמִית to slay David without cause , 25:31 ; Psa 35:7 (twice in verse); 109:3 ; 119:161 חִנָּם רְדָפוּנִי , Prov 1:11 ; 3:30 ; 23:29 ; Job 2:3 ח ׳לְבַלְּעוֺ 9:17 ; 22:6 ; Ezek 14:23 ; Psa 35:19 ; and 69:5 חִנָּם שׂנְאַי my haters without cause , Lam 3:52 חִנָּם אֹיְבַי ; in the Genitive 1Kin 2:31 חִנָּם דְּמֵי blood shed without cause (compare 1Sam 25:31 ), Prov 24:28 בְּרֵעֶ֑ךָ ח עֵד ׳אֲלתְּֿהִי , 26:2 ח ׳קִלְלַת the causeless curse.","rootNote":"from 2580 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 21 24","keyReferences":["1Chr 21 24","1Kgs 2 31","1Sam 19 5","1Sam 25 31","2Sam 24 24","Exod 21 2","Exod 21 11","Ezek 6 10"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":32,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 21 24","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חִנָּֽם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Kgs 2 31","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":31,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חִנָּ֗ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Sam 19 5","book":"1Sam","chapter":19,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חִנָּֽם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Sam 25 31","book":"1Sam","chapter":25,"verse":31,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חִנָּ֔ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"2Sam 24 24","book":"2Sam","chapter":24,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חִנָּ֑ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"Exod 21 2","book":"Exod","chapter":21,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חִנָּֽם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"Exod 21 11","book":"Exod","chapter":21,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חִנָּ֖ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"Ezek 6 10","book":"Ezek","chapter":6,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חִנָּם֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"Ezek 14 23","book":"Ezek","chapter":14,"verse":23,"englishText":